    "releaseNotes": "2.5.4 - With SLAM on, a manual FC target now works as the SLAM target. Before this release the app treated SLAM on with a manual target as outside SLAM, so a target above 10 was capped to 10.0 ppm and a WaterGuru very high alert held the pump. Now a manual target (above 0, at most 50 ppm) is used as entered: only the SLAM checks apply (a 0.0 reading, a drop of more than 4 ppm, an exact 10.0) and the pump limits. It is not limited to the SLAM factor times CYA. The advice and the settings page say SLAM and name the target. With SLAM off nothing changes: a manual target above 10 is capped to 10.0 ppm. Code update only, no need to press Done.",
